      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>Coming back to Squeak from another Space no longer flips a finished chat to Idle and back.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.29.1</h4><ul><li>New threads really start in Skip approvals now: picking a preset no longer switches them back to Ask.</li><li>Only one "Next update" button above the composer (two could stack up).</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.29.0</h4><ul><li>Every stream's tab strip starts with a small pinned tab: the pond room. It shows what each thread in the pond is working on right now, as short lines rather than every edit and command, plus "needs you" and "finished" notes. Turn on "Show agent talk" to see threads coordinating with each other, and type in it to talk to the room like a group chat.</li><li>Adding your iPhone or a browser is just signing in with the same account: the QR code and pairing codes are gone from Settings and setup.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
